  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following statements:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. Atoms of each element emit characteristics spectrum.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> According to Bohr&#39;s Postulate, an electron in a hydrogen atom&nbsp;revolves in a certain stationary orbit.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The density of nuclear matter depends on the size of the nucleus.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;A free neutron is stable but a free proton decay is possible.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Radioactivity is an indication of the instability of nuclei. Choose the correct answer from the options given below.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7GZ4C",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">,</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">,</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">,</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi>D</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math>",
